# Change Log

## 4.0.0

### Added

- Third-party storage support: 100 operations that address a file, folder or room (for example `getFileInfo`, `getFolderByFolderId`, `updateRoom`, `uploadFile`, the sharing and upload-session operations) have two overloads, one taking the identifier as an `Int` and one as a `String`: the `Int` overload addresses an entry stored on the portal, and the `String` overload an entry in a connected third-party storage (for example `"sbox-42"`); the 39 of them that return a file, folder or upload session return the matching `ThirdParty*` model from the `String` overload (`ThirdPartyFileWrapper`, `ThirdPartyFolderWrapper`, `ThirdPartyFolderContentWrapper`, `ThirdPartyChunkedUploadSessionWrapper` and others), and `saveFileAsPdf` and `startFileConversion` take `ThirdPartySaveAsPdfRequest` and `ThirdPartyCheckConversionRequestDto` there
- Added the reworked AI API in `Sources/OpenAPIClient/APIs/AI/`: `AIAIAPIApi` (sending messages with or without streaming, regenerating answers, approving and denying tool calls), `AIAssignmentsAPIApi`, `AIAttachmentsAPIApi`, `AIContextAPIApi`, `AIEditorToolsAPIApi`, `AIExportAPIApi`, `AIOpenAIPassthroughAPIApi`, `AIPreferencesAPIApi`, `AIProfilesAPIApi`, `AIPromptsAPIApi`, `AIThreadsAPIApi`, `AIToolsAPIApi` and `AIWebSearchAPIApi`; `AISettingsAPIApi` gains `aiSettingsGetUser`, `aiSettingsSetUser`, `aiSettingsGetToolMode` and `aiSettingsSetToolMode` with the models `AiUserSettingsDto` and `AiUserSettingsWrapper`
- Added `FilesMetadataAPIApi` (`APIs/Files/MetadataAPI.swift`): metadata templates and their fields, assigning templates to files and folders, custom fields and field values; the new `searchFolder` (`FilesFoldersAPIApi`) and `searchRooms` (`RoomsAPIApi`) find entries by their metadata, and files and folders carry `assignedMetadataTemplates` and `metadataMatches`
- Added `AppsAPIApi` (`APIs/Apps/`), `RoomsPrivacyRoomAPIApi` (`APIs/Rooms/PrivacyRoomAPI.swift`, the users' encryption keys for privacy rooms) and `SettingsDocsCloudAPIApi` (`APIs/Settings/DocsCloudAPI.swift`)
- Added the operations `getFormsFolder` (`FilesFoldersAPIApi`), `getRoomAiFolder`, `startExternalDbSync` and `getExternalDbSyncStatus` (`RoomsAPIApi`), `showQuickActions` and `changeExternalSharingSettings` (`FilesSettingsAPIApi`), `getEncryptionInfo` and `setEncryptionInfo` (`FilesFilesAPIApi`) and `getEncryptionAccess` (`FilesSharingAPIApi`)
- Report generation: `createReportFolderHistory`, `createAuditTrailReport` and `createLoginHistoryReport` take `format`, `from` and `to` and return a `DocumentBuilderTaskWrapper`; the new `getReportFolderHistory`, `getAuditTrailReport`, `getLoginHistoryReport` and the matching `terminate*` operations follow and cancel the report
- Added the payment operations `getActiveServices`, `getAccountingServicePrices`, `getSubscriptionBalanceInfo`, `moveSubscriptionToWallet`, `getCustomerServiceUsage` and `getCustomerMonthlyUsage` with their `create*Report`, `get*Report` and `terminate*Report` operations (`PortalPaymentAPIApi`), and `getUpcomingPayments` (`PortalQuotaAPIApi`)
- Added `getBackupsCounts` (`BackupAPIApi`) and `refreshWebPlugin` (`SettingsWebpluginsAPIApi`)
- The response field filter is the `fields` parameter of the 18 operations that support it (for example `AIAgentsAPIApi.aiAgentsList(..., fields: "id,title")`, `FilesFoldersAPIApi.getMyFolder(..., fields: ...)`), sent as the `fields` header; it replaces `withFields`, an instance method of three AI API classes that the static API methods could not use
- Added model properties: `sharedExternal` to files, folders and `FileEntryBaseDto`, `resultsFolderId` and `externalDbTableName` to `FileDto`, `originalFormId` to `FolderDto`, `sendFormToExternalDB` and `saveFormAsXLSX` to `CreateRoomRequestDto`, `showQuickActions`, `defaultShareLinkInternal`, `externalShareApplyToDocuments`, `externalShareApplyToRooms` and `blockExistingLinksOnRestrict` to `FilesSettingsDto`, `formsUsedSpace` to `FilesStatisticsResultDto`, `ai` to `CustomizationConfigDto`, `isDelayedPaymentMethod` and `paymentMethodType` to `CustomerInfoDto`, `searchArea` to `RoomGroupDto` and `RoomGroupRequestDto`, `walletLowBalance` to `SettingsDto`, `runtime` to `WebPluginDto`, `toolPermissionMode` and `recommendedModelForForms` to `AiSettingsDto`, `lastModified` to `TenantAiAccessSettingsDto`, `TenantBannerSettingsDto` and `TenantDevToolsAccessSettingsDto`, `errors` to `ProblemDetail`; `OperationDto` describes the source of a charge with `sourceId`, `sourceTitle`, `sourceType`, `cost`, `tokenUsage` and `type` instead of `agentId` and `agentTitle`, and `EditorToolCallStateDto.parameters` is an `EditorToolCallParametersDto` instead of a `JSONValue`
- Added enum values: `FolderType.Forms` (36) and `FolderType.Ai` (37); `SearchArea.forms` and `SearchArea.formTemplates`; `TenantWalletService.Admin`, `DocsCloud`, `DocsCloudDevPack` and `AISearch`; `OperationType.AiServicePayment`, `AiDebit` and `AiCredit`; new audit actions in `MessageAction` (privacy room keys, metadata templates and values, AI profiles, Docs Cloud and others)
- Added the error body models `ErrorApiResponse` and `ValidationErrorResponse` (with `FieldError`)
- Added a usage sample in `samples/docspace-api-sdk-swift-sample/`: a Swift package that builds against the SDK in this repository and signs in, creates, renames and deletes a folder, lists the rooms and starts a backup; run it with `swift run` from that folder after setting the portal address and credentials in `Sources/Sample/main.swift`

### Changed

- Files, folders and rooms use one set of models for numeric identifiers: the `Integer` suffix is gone (`FileIntegerWrapper` → `FileWrapper`, `FolderIntegerWrapper` → `FolderWrapper`, `FolderContentIntegerWrapper` → `FolderContentWrapper`, `FileDtoInteger` → `FileDto`, `FolderDtoInteger` → `FolderDto`, `FileEntryDtoInteger` → `FileEntryDto`, `ConfigurationIntegerWrapper` → `ConfigurationWrapper`, `UploadSessionResponseIntegerWrapper` → `UploadSessionResponseWrapper`, `OrdersRequestDtoInteger` → `OrdersRequestDto`, `UpdateRoomsQuotaRequestDtoInteger` → `UpdateRoomsQuotaRequestDto`, `SaveAsPdfInteger` → `SaveAsPdfRequest` and so on), and the `String` variants became `ThirdParty*` models (`FolderStringWrapper` → `ThirdPartyFolderWrapper`, `FolderDtoString` → `ThirdPartyFolderDto`, `FileEntryDtoString` → `ThirdPartyFileEntryDto`); the chunked-upload operations return `ChunkedUploadSessionWrapper` and `ChunkedUploadSessionResultWrapper`; the nested share models of files and folders are `AiFileEntryDtoAllOfShareSettings`, `AiFileEntryDtoAllOfSecurity` and `AiFileEntryDtoAllOfAvailableShareRights` (were `FolderDtoIntegerShareSettings`, `FolderDtoIntegerSecurity` and `FolderDtoIntegerAvailableShareRights`)
- Renamed the request models with the plural `Requests` to the singular (`AuthRequestsDto` → `AuthRequestDto`, `SsoSettingsRequestsDto` → `SsoSettingsRequestDto`, `TfaRequestsDto` → `TfaRequestDto`, `StorageRequestsDto` → `StorageRequestDto`, `CspRequestsDto` → `CspRequestDto`, `WhiteLabelRequestsDto` → `WhiteLabelRequestDto`, `WebPluginRequests` → `WebPluginRequest` and the rest), and the JSON bodies nested in a request take a `Request` suffix (`Delete` → `DeleteFileRequest`, `DeleteFolder` → `DeleteFolderRequest`, `CreateFolder` → `CreateFolderRequest`, `CreateFileJsonElement` → `CreateFileRequest`, `CreateTextOrHtmlFile` → `CreateTextOrHtmlFileRequest`, `CopyAsJsonElement` → `CopyAsRequest`, `UpdateFile` → `UpdateFileRequest`, `UpdateComment` → `UpdateCommentRequest`, `ChangeHistory` → `ChangeHistoryRequest`, `CheckFillFormDraft` → `CheckFillFormDraftRequest`, `CustomFilterParameters` → `CustomFilterRequest`, `CreateThirdPartyRoom` → `CreateThirdPartyRoomRequest`, `LockFileParameters` → `LockFileRequest`, `StartEdit` → `StartEditRequest`, `Culture` → `UpdateMemberCultureRequest`, `MentionMessageWrapper` → `MentionMessageRequest`, `EmailValidationKeyModel` → `CheckConfirmRequestDto`); the JSON sent is unchanged
- The argument label of a request body is the name of its model, so the labels changed with the models: `authenticateMe(authRequestsDto:)` → `authenticateMe(authRequestDto:)`, `createFile(folderId:createFileJsonElement:)` → `createFile(folderId:createFileRequest:)`, `setTenantWalletSettings(tenantWalletSettingsWrapper:)` → `setTenantWalletSettings(tenantWalletSettingsRequestDto:)`, `startBackup(backupDto:)` → `startBackup(startBackupRequestDto:)`, `updateMemberCulture(userid:culture:)` → `updateMemberCulture(userId:updateMemberCultureRequest:)`, `changeDefaultAccessRights(requestBody:)` → `changeDefaultAccessRights(defaultAccessRightsRequestDto:)`, `deleteTemplates(requestBody:)` → `deleteTemplates(deleteTemplateFilesRequestDto:)` and so on
- Path parameters are spelled in camel case, which changes their argument labels: `userid` → `userId` (`getProfileByUserId`, `updateMember`, `deleteMember`, `changeUserEmail`, `changeUserPassword`, the photo operations, `getGroupByUserId`, `getGuestSharingLink`, the reassign, remove and user type progress operations), `userID` → `userId` (`getUserById`), `productid` → `productId` and `userid` → `userId` (`getIsProductAdministrator`, `getProductAdministrators`), `activationstatus` → `activationStatus` (`updateUserActivationStatus`); `setFileSecurityInfo` and `setFolderSecurityInfo` take the entry as `id` instead of `fileId` and `folderId`
- Settings, database entities and other server-side classes are no longer published as models: each one became a `Dto` of the same shape (`TenantQuota` → `TenantQuotaDto`, `Balance` → `BalanceDto`, `Tariff` → `TariffDto`, `BackupProgress` → `BackupProgressDto`, `CoEditingConfig` → `CoEditingConfigDto`, `Logo` → `LogoDto`, `StorageSettings` and `CdnStorageSettings` → `StorageSettingsDto`, `DarkThemeSettings` → `DarkThemeSettingsDto`, `WizardSettings` → `WizardSettingsDto`, the editor configuration models `PermissionsConfig`, `EmbeddedConfig`, `UserConfig`, `FeedbackConfig` and the rest → `*ConfigDto` and so on) or a model named after what it carries (`UserInfo` → `PortalUserDto`, `FireBaseUser` → `FirebaseDeviceDto`, `ThirdPartyParams` → `ThirdPartyAccountDto`, `CompanyWhiteLabelSettings` → `LicensorDetailsDto`, `AdditionalWhiteLabelSettings` → `AdditionalResourcesDto`, `SsoSettingsV2` → `SsoSettingsDto`, `IPRestriction` → `IpRestrictionDto`, `IpRestrictionBase` → `IpRestrictionEntryDto`, `SetupCode` → `TfaSetupCodeDto`, `IMagickGeometry` → `WhiteLabelItemSizeDto`, `PasswordHasher` → `PasswordHashSettingsDto`, `TenantDomainValidator` → `DomainNameRulesDto`, `CultureSpecificExternalResources` → `ExternalResourcesDto`, `TenantEntityQuotaSettings` → `EntityQuotaDto`); the room, user and AI agent quota settings are all returned as `EntityQuotaSettingsWrapper`
- The settings sent in a request body take the name of their operation and keep every field (`TenantWalletSettingsWrapper` → `TenantWalletSettingsRequestDto` with `SetWalletTopUpSettingsRequest`, `TenantAuditSettingsWrapper` → `TenantAuditSettingsRequestDto` with `SetAuditLifetimeSettingsRequest`, `CompanyWhiteLabelSettingsWrapper` → `CompanyWhiteLabelSettingsRequestDto` with `SaveCompanyInfoRequest`, `AdditionalWhiteLabelSettingsWrapper` → `AdditionalWhiteLabelSettingsRequestDto` with `SaveAdditionalResourcesRequest`, `TenantAiAccessSettingsDto` → `TenantAiAccessSettingsRequestDto`, `TenantBannerSettingsDto` → `TenantBannerSettingsRequestDto`, `TenantDevToolsAccessSettingsDto` → `TenantDevToolsAccessSettingsRequestDto`, `ExternalDatabaseSettings` → `ExternalDatabaseConnectionRequestDto`, `EmailActivationSettings` → `EmailActivationSettingsRequestDto`); `TenantWalletSettingsWrapper`, `TenantAuditSettingsWrapper`, `CompanyWhiteLabelSettingsWrapper` and `AdditionalWhiteLabelSettingsWrapper` return the settings in `response` instead of a `settings` property; `saveAuthKeys` takes `SaveAuthKeysRequestDto` and `getAuthServices` returns `AuthServiceArrayWrapper`
- Renamed other models whose names did not say what they carry: `Status` → `ExternalShareStatus`, `Options` → `DocumentOptionsDto`, `STRINGArrayWrapper` → `StringArrayWrapper`, `EncryprtionStatus` → `EncryptionStatus`, `AceShortWrapper` → `AceShortDto`, `MentionWrapper` → `MentionDto`, `TimezonesRequestsDto` → `TimezoneDto`, `GroupMemberSecurityRequestDto` → `GroupMemberSecurityDto`, `SmtpOperationStatusRequestsDto` → `SmtpOperationStatusDto`, `KeyValuePairBooleanString` → `ItemKeyValuePairBooleanString`, `HistoryData` → `HistoryDataDto`, `HistoryAction` → `HistoryActionDto`, `Area` → `AccountSearchArea`, `Location` → `RequestLocation`, `TfaRequestsDtoType` → `TfaType`, `DraftLocationInteger` → `DraftLocation`, and the backup request models after their operation (`BackupDto` → `StartBackupRequestDto`, `BackupRestoreDto` → `StartBackupRestoreRequestDto`, `BackupScheduleDto` → `CreateBackupScheduleRequestDto`, `Cron` → `BackupCronRequest`, `CronParams` → `CronParamsDto`)
- Operations that returned an untyped `ObjectWrapper` or `ObjectArrayWrapper` now return a typed model: `StringWrapper` (`getPortalPath`, `getPortalHostname`, `getGreetingSettings`, `getThirdPartyCode`), `StringArrayWrapper` (`getRoomTagsInfo`), `FileArrayWrapper` (`uploadFile`, `uploadFileToMy`), `TokenDiagnosticsWrapper` (`getClaims`), `AuditTrailProductArrayWrapper` (`getAuditTrailMappers`), `AuditTrailTypesWrapper` (`getAuditTrailTypes`), `EnabledModuleArrayWrapper` (`getEnabledModules`), `SocketSettingsWrapper` (`getSocketSettings`), `SsoSettingsConstantsWrapper` (`getSsoSettingsV2Constants`), `AmazonS3RegionArrayWrapper` (`getAmazonS3Regions`), `AccountEntryArrayWrapper` (`getAccountsEntriesWith*Shared`)
- Other return types: `deleteFileVersions` returns `FileOperationArrayWrapper`, `searchUsersByQuery` returns `EmployeeFullArrayWrapper`, `checkUserExistsByEmail` returns `UserExistsResponseWrapper`, `changeDefaultAccessRights` returns `FileShareResponseArrayWrapper`, `updateCdnStorage` returns `StorageSettingsWrapper`, `getWebhookTriggers` returns `WebhookTriggerArrayWrapper`, `getAiPrices` returns `AiPricesWrapper`, `getRestrictedAiModels` and `setRestrictedAiModels` return `RestrictedAiModelsWrapper`; `deleteGroup` and `deleteRecent` return nothing; `getTfaConfirmUrl` is now `getTfaConfirmData` and returns `TfaConfirmDataWrapper` instead of `StringWrapper`; in Files, `changeDownloadZipFromBody` → `changeDownloadZip`
- `uploadFile` and `uploadFileToMy` send the file as multipart form data with the separate parameters `file` (a `URL`), `createNewIfExist`, `storeOriginalFile` and `keepConvertStatus` instead of one `UploadRequestDto`
- Renamed the AI agent operations after their tag, so the method names change: `createAgent` → `aiAgentsCreate`, `getAgents` → `aiAgentsList`, `getAgentInfo` → `aiAgentsGet`, `getAgentsNewItems` → `aiAgentsNews`, `updateAgent` → `aiAgentsUpdate`, `deleteAgent` → `aiAgentsDelete`, `updateAgentsQuota` → `aiAgentsUpdateQuota`, `resetAgentsQuota` → `aiAgentsResetQuota`, `getAiSettings` → `aiSettingsGet`, `getVectorizationSettings` → `aiSettingsGetVectorization`, `setVectorizationSettings` → `aiSettingsSetVectorization`, `startTask` → `aiVectorizationStartTask`
- The AI agent operations take the agent `id` as a `String` and use their own `Ai`-prefixed models (`AiFolderWrapper`, `AiFolderContentWrapper`, `AiFileOperationWrapper`, `AiAgentsCreateRequest`, `AiAgentsUpdateRequest` and others) instead of the models of the Files API; their request bodies are required; `aiAgentsList` takes `quotaFilter` as an `Int` and `sortOrder` as a `String`; `aiSettingsSetUser` and `aiSettingsSetVectorization` take the settings as a `[String: JSONValue?]`; `AiSettingsDto` and `AiSettingsWrapper` keep their names but describe the reworked AI settings
- The OAuth 2.0 client and scope operations call `/api/2.0/oauth2/clients` and `/api/2.0/oauth2/scopes` instead of `/api/2.0/clients` and `/api/2.0/scopes`; `getClients` returns `PageableClientResponse` instead of `PageableResponse` and its `limit` is optional, `getClientsInfo` returns `PageableClientInfoResponse` (renamed from `PageableResponseClientInfoResponse`), `getScopes` returns `[ScopeResponse]` instead of one `ScopeResponse`, and `changeActivation`, `deleteClient`, `deleteTenantClients`, `deleteUserClients`, `revokeUserClient`, `updateClient` and `handleOptions` return nothing instead of a `JSONValue`; `CreateClientRequest` requires `name`, `logo`, `scopes`, `websiteUrl`, `termsUrl`, `policyUrl` and `logoutRedirectUri`, and `UpdateClientRequest` requires `name`, `logo`, `allowedOrigins`, `scopes` and `redirectUris`
- `checkMoveOrCopyBatchItems` and `checkMoveOrCopyDestFolder` take the batch as separate query parameters (`returnSingleOperation`, `folderIds`, `fileIds`, `destFolderId`, `conflictResolveType`, `deleteAfter`, `content`, `toFillOut`) instead of one `inDto` object, which is how the server reads them
- New and changed parameters: the folder listings `getMyFolder`, `getFavoritesFolder`, `getRecentFolder`, `getTrashFolder`, `getFolderByFolderId` and `getRoomsFolder` take `metadataTemplateId` and `metadataFilters`; `getFolderByFolderId` also takes `folderType` and `withSubFolders`, and its `location` is a `RequestLocation`; `getRoomsFolder` takes `subjectId` and `subjectOwnerId` as `UUID`, no longer takes `subjectFilter` and takes `privacyFilter` and `withAiFolder`; `emptyTrash` takes `folderType` and `getPaymentQuotas` takes `additional`; `getRoomGroups` no longer takes the required `id` argument and takes `searchArea`; `getCheckoutSetupUrl` requires `backUrl` and the new `successUrl`, and `PaymentUrlRequestDto` requires `backUrl`, `quantity` and `successUrl`; `getCustomerOperations` takes `serviceName` as `[String]` and one `type` instead of `types`, and no longer takes `writeOffServiceQuota`
- Parameter and property types: the date filters of `getFileHistory`, `getFolderHistory`, `getAuditEventsByFilter` and `getLoginEventsByFilter` are `Date` instead of `ApiDateTime`; `TariffDto.dueDate`, `delayDueDate` and `licenseDate` and `TariffQuotaDto.dueDate` are `ApiDateTime` instead of `Date`; `EditorConfigurationDto.encryptionKeys` is `[EncryptionKeyDto]` instead of `EncryptionKeysConfig`; `GroupRequestDto.groupManager` is optional, while `LogoRequest.tmpFile`, `RoomTemplateDto.title` and the fields of `SalesRequestDto` are required
- `SearchArea` is a `String` enum sent and received as a string instead of a number, and its cases are in lower camel case (`SearchArea.Active` → `.active`, `.RecentByLinks` → `.recentByLinks`, `.AiAgents` → `.aiAgents`, ...); `FolderType.ResultStorage` (33) is now `FolderType.ChatOutputs`
- `OperationStatus` and `OperationType` are numbered in sequence instead of as flags, so the numbers sent and received change: `OperationStatus` is `Pending` (0), `Completed` (1), `Rejected` (2), `Canceled` (3), and `OperationType` runs from `Unknown` (0) to `AiCredit` (19); the `Any` case of both is gone
- The 19 API files whose name repeated in another folder take the folder as a prefix (`Files/QuotaAPI.swift` → `Files/FilesQuotaAPI.swift`, `People/SearchAPI.swift` → `People/PeopleSearchAPI.swift`, `AI/SettingsAPI.swift` → `AI/AISettingsAPI.swift`, and so on for every `QuotaAPI`, `SearchAPI`, `SettingsAPI`, `ProfilesAPI`, `GuestsAPI`, `AuthorizationAPI`, `AccessToDevToolsAPI` and `BannersVisibilityAPI`)
- The `Type` case of `SortedByType` is `_Type`: a case named `Type` cannot be declared in Swift
- Regenerated with OpenAPI Generator 7.24.0 (previously 7.21.0)

### Fixed

- The package builds: every API class is declared under its name (`AIAgentsAPIApi`, `FilesQuotaAPIApi`, ...) instead of an unfilled template placeholder, and SwiftPM no longer stops on two source files with the same name
- Arrays of integer enums (`FilesSettingsDto.DefaultSharingAccessRights`, `TenantWalletServiceSettingsDto.EnabledServices`, the `employeeTypes` filters of `getSimpleByFilter` and `searchUsersByExtendedFilter`) have `Int` raw values instead of `String`
- Models that take one of several types (`anyOf`: the `folderIds`/`fileIds` items of the batch file operations such as `BaseBatchRequestDtoAllOfFileIds`, `DownloadRequestDtoAllOfFolderIds`, `DeleteBatchRequestDtoAllOfFileIds`) are enums with a case per type; they were empty structs that could not be created outside the module and were sent as `{}`
- Validation patterns are plain regular expressions without `/.../` delimiters, so `StringRule` accepts valid values (a `color` of `ff0000`) and the models with patterns compile
- Dates (`ApiDateTime`: `created`, `updated`, `expirationDate` and the rest) are read from and sent as the ISO 8601 string the portal uses (`2026-10-15T14:00:00.0000000+03:00`), filling `utcTime` and `timeZoneOffset`; every answer with a date failed to decode, because the model expected an object

### Removed

- Removed the superseded AI API classes `ChatAPI`, `MCPAPI`, `MessagesAPI` and `ProvidersAPI` from `Sources/OpenAPIClient/APIs/AI/` together with their models (`ChatDto`, `MessageDto`, `McpServerDto`, `AiProviderDto`, `ModelDto`, `UserChatSettingsDto`, `WebSearchSettingsDto` and others); the web search settings moved from `getWebSearchSettings`/`setWebSearchSettings` to `AIWebSearchAPIApi`
- Removed the request models `SetEmbeddingConfigRequestBody` and `VectorizationStartRequestBody`, the `AiSettingsDto` properties that described the old AI chat (`webSearchEnabled`, `webSearchNeedReset`, `aiReadyNeedReset`, `portalMcpServerId`, `modelAliases`, the `*ToolName` properties) and the model properties of `ChatSettingsDto` (`providerId`, `modelId`, `modelAlias`, `capabilities`, `multimodal`, `thinking`, `_internal`)
- Removed `getPrivacyFolder` (Files), `isAvailablePrivacyRoomSettings` (Files settings), `buyWalletService` and `getCustomerServiceQuota` (Payment)
- Removed the `subjectFilter` parameter of `getRoomsFolder` and `aiAgentsList` with its `SubjectFilter` enum, the `MessageAction` cases `PrivacyRoomEnable` and `PrivacyRoomDisable`, and the `_public` property of the OAuth 2.0 client models
- Removed the server-side models that no operation uses any more: `DbTenant`, `DbTenantPartner`, `AuthData`, `OAuth20Token`, `NoContentResult`, `NoContentResultWrapper`, `StatusCodeResult`, `ObjectWrapper`, `UnknownWrapper`, `UploadRequestDto`, `ContentDisposition` and `ContentType`
- The third-party accounts returned by `getThirdPartyAccounts` no longer have the `authData` property, and the devices returned by `docRegisterPusnNotificationDevice` and `subscribeDocumentsPushNotification` no longer have `tenant`; neither was ever filled in

